When a sentence has several extra pieces, the usual order is **time (wann?) → manner (wie?) → place (wo/wohin?)**. Teachers call it *Te-Ka-Mo-Lo* (temporal, kausal, modal, lokal):

{de:Hans fährt **morgen** **mit dem Bus** **in die Schule**.}

{de:Lisa geht **am Dienstag** **zu Fuß** **ins Kino**.}

You can put one piece first for emphasis — the verb stays in position 2: {de:Am Dienstag geht Lisa zu Fuß ins Kino.}
